---
title: Example · Semantic version grammar
config:
  look: classic
  theme: dark
  railroad:
    specialStroke: "#b3b3b3"
---
%% Other notations: `railroad-abnf-beta` (railroad-abnf), `railroad-peg-beta` (railroad-peg), `railroad-beta` IR constructors (railroad-ir).
%% EBNF: `a b` or `a , b` sequence · `a | b` choice · `[ a ]` or `a?` optional · `{ a }` or `a*` zero or more · `a+` one or more · `( … )` group · `"x"` or `'x'` terminal · `? … ?` prose · `(* … *)` or `/* … */` comment; rules take `=` or `::=`.
%% `a - b` (except) draws the minus as a literal terminal, reading as a, a hyphen, then b, so state an exclusion as `? … ?` prose.
railroad-ebnf-beta
title "Example · Semantic version grammar"
version = core [ "-" prerelease ] [ "+" build ] ;
core = number "." number "." number ;
number = "0" | nonzero { digit } ;
prerelease = identifier { "." identifier } ;
(* build metadata never affects precedence *)
build = identifier ( "." identifier )* ;
identifier = ( letter | digit | "-" )+ ;
nonzero = ? digit 1 to 9 ? ;
digit = "0" | nonzero ;
letter = ? ASCII letter ? ;
